From 798af188405517f5b6b350246c27c59e199db883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: b70-notes <b70-notes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:08:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] DSpark for Inkling 2 (inkling2 / inkling2_loop targets)
 on master: port of the Unsloth b12572-mix graph, greedy drafting

- dflash: BACKBONE_INKLING2 (dspark.markov_rank > 0): load_hparams/tensors_inkling2, graph_inkling2 (context K/V
  injection from mixed target features, 3-layer noncausal block backbone, recurrent markov head); the target's
  embeddings and lm head are shared via ctx_other. Tensor names dspark_fuse/dspark_norm/dspark_hidden_out,
  blk.N.{dflare_norm,attn_k_ctx,attn_v_ctx,attn_k_ctx_norm}; KV dflash.dspark.markov_rank.
- inkling2 graph: t_layer_inp[e] = input of layer pass e in execution order (a looped core pass counts once per
  pass), t_layer_inp[n_layer] = final normed hidden; these are the DSpark target features (layers 5/23/41/48).
- llama-batch: dspark drafters take an embd state per token (the committed anchor's context feature).
- speculative: Inkling DSpark driver (context feature store, full-block decode, first-max host sampling);
  probabilistic drafting is not ported and is refused. LLAMA_SPEC_TIMING=N prints host time per step.
- Faster than the Unsloth original: the markov head runs only for the drafted positions (LLAMA_DSPARK_NCHAIN,
  set from --spec-draft-n-max), the backbone logits are folded into each chained position's single lm-head
  pass (LLAMA_DSPARK_FOLD=0: old two-pass form), and the next-token choice is a plain argmax instead of the
  pool_1d first-maximum construction (one work-item scanned the 200k vocabulary per position on SYCL;
  LLAMA_DSPARK_ARGMAX=0: old form). Draft step 2.4 ms at n-max 1 (Unsloth original ~37 ms).
- SYCL argmax: ties go to the lowest column (first maximum, as on the CPU).

